From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:18:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 54/86] Session restore keeps each view's scroll position

Restoring the cursor marked it as moved, so the first layout scrolled the
view to the cursor before the editor knew its height and the saved scroll
was lost. With two synchronized views, the view with a cursor further down
jumped and the views no longer lined up. The restored cursor is now shaped
before the saved scroll is set, so both views come back where they were
and that is the baseline for synchronized scrolling.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

